use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../Menu import Menu

export ui-component ContextMenu:
    description:
        A context menu is a Menu that opens where the user right-clicks, or
        long-presses on a touch screen, inside some area, such as a file in a
        list. It offers actions for the thing that was clicked, in place of the
        platform's own menu.

    composes:
        - @{Menu}

    opening:
        Right-clicking inside the area opens the menu at the pointer, in place
        of the platform's own menu. On touch screens and with a pen, pressing
        and holding for a moment opens it; letting go early or moving away
        doesn't. From the keyboard, the platform's usual key for this, such as
        the context menu key or Shift+F10, opens it beside whatever is focused.
        The first item is current when it opens.

    position:
        It opens with a corner at the point that was clicked, and Positioning
        keeps it on screen from there. Right-clicking somewhere else in the
        area while it's open moves it there.

    target:
        The component is told where in the area the menu was opened, so it can
        offer actions for that thing, such as the file under the pointer.

    closing:
        It closes the way a Menu does. Focus then goes back to whatever had it
        before the menu opened.

    everythingElse:
        Items, submenus, ticked and picked options, and moving around all work
        as in a Menu.

    nonGoals:
        - Nothing in it is available only there. Right-clicking and long-pressing
            are hard to discover, so every action also has another way in
        - No button opens it. A menu opened from a button is a Menu
